{
  "name": "UberLLM: UGC-style product ad from one product photo",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## UGC-style product ad (UberLLM)\nFrom one product photo to a vertical ad clip of a person holding your product:\n1. **Plan the ad**: a vision model (`google/gemini-2.5-flash`) looks at the photo and writes the scene, the motion, a hook and a caption.\n2. **Make UGC scene**: `google/nano-banana-2-edit` puts your product in a creator's hand (the label stays as it is).\n3. **Start ad video**: `fal-ai/kling-video/v3/standard/image-to-video` turns that picture into a 5 s clip with sound.\n\n### Setup (2 minutes)\n1. Get a key at https://uberllm.dev (sign in with your email, add credit).\n2. Open any **UberLLM** HTTP node → Credential → **Create new** → *Header Auth*:\n   - Name: `Authorization`\n   - Value: `Bearer YOUR_UBERLLM_KEY`\n   Every UberLLM node in this workflow uses this one credential.\n3. Edit the **Settings** node, then click **Execute workflow**.\n\n`product_image_url` must be a public `https://` link to the product photo (a plain background works best). If you change `vision_model`, pick one that reads pictures from a link (`google/gemini-2.5-flash` does).\n\n### Price\nScene picture $0.07 + 5 s clip with sound $0.5355 = about $0.6055 per ad (prices on 2026-10-30). The planning call costs a fraction of a cent.\n\n### What you pay\n- The job's cost is shown before it starts (`max_cost_usd` on the reply) and held from your balance. It is never billed more than that.\n- A video that fails or runs out of time costs nothing: the whole hold comes back.\n- Credit you buy does not expire.\n- No UberLLM fee on requests. Adding credit by card costs 5.5% + $0.50.\n\n### The file\nThe last node has the video as binary `data` (send it to Drive, S3, YouTube…) and its link in `url`. The link needs your key and is kept about 3 hours. To have UberLLM put the file in your own bucket, add `output_upload_url` (a presigned PUT link) to the start request.\n",
        "height": 980,
        "width": 560
      },
